1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:04,300
I've got twenty minutes before I'm due back.

2
00:00:04,600 --> 00:00:07,400
Okay. What have you got?

3
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:16,300
Three cases. That's all I can give you.

4
00:00:16,600 --> 00:00:21,800
Receipt here, missing paperwork here. Same code on all three.

5
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:26,350
How many more look like this?

6
00:00:26,650 --> 00:00:31,750
I checked these three. I'm not giving you a number I don't have.

7
00:00:32,050 --> 00:00:35,580
Can I talk to the doctors who signed them?

8
00:00:35,880 --> 00:00:37,840
You'll have to ask them.

9
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:48,200
I reported it. Got a ticket number. Never heard back.

10
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:53,800
Signed off without opening the files?

11
00:00:54,100 --> 00:01:00,800
I haven't seen the viewing logs. Don't say I told you that.

12
00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:07,710
Then how does a file get signed off with the paperwork missing?

13
00:01:08,010 --> 00:01:12,320
That's what I asked in the report. It isn't an answer.

14
00:01:12,620 --> 00:01:15,760
Okay. You haven't seen them. I've got it.

15
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:23,800
You can trace that right to me.

16
00:01:24,100 --> 00:01:26,900
Okay. Dates only?

17
00:01:27,200 --> 00:01:29,500
And the report number.

18
00:01:32,000 --> 00:01:34,800
This number gets us the report?

19
00:01:35,100 --> 00:01:39,400
It should. They never sent me a response.

20
00:01:44,000 --> 00:01:46,300
Luigi had this page.

21
00:01:46,600 --> 00:01:52,300
I sent it to the appeal group. He offered to help.

22
00:01:56,000 --> 00:01:57,570
Did you meet him?

23
00:01:57,870 --> 00:02:01,790
No. Messages. Mostly people asking where to send an appeal.

24
00:02:02,090 --> 00:02:04,050
Can you show me those?

25
00:02:04,350 --> 00:02:07,490
Not here. Not before I talk to someone.

26
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:18,800
Don't put me in a story about him.

27
00:02:19,100 --> 00:02:24,300
I won't name you. But I have to mention the group.

28
00:02:24,600 --> 00:02:27,900
I didn't know anything about a gun.

29
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:35,700
Did anyone actually see a doctor skip a file?

30
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:41,200
No. Three receipts, three denials. Nobody will explain it.

31
00:02:43,000 --> 00:02:48,880
Three families sent records. The insurer says they were missing. We can prove that much.

32
00:02:49,180 --> 00:02:54,670
That's the letter they already got. We need to say what happened to them.

33
00:03:03,000 --> 00:03:05,800
They say clinicians reviewed them.

34
00:03:06,100 --> 00:03:10,400
Use it. They still haven't sent the logs.

35
00:03:13,000 --> 00:03:18,100
Not sending us a log isn't the same as nobody opening a file.

36
00:03:18,400 --> 00:03:21,930
Then they can show us one. We've asked twice.

37
00:03:22,230 --> 00:03:24,970
I'm asking what you can show me.

38
00:03:33,000 --> 00:03:36,530
Three times. Same missing-materials code. I'm keeping the line.

39
00:03:36,830 --> 00:03:39,970
Keep their response beside it. Don't bury it.

40
00:03:40,270 --> 00:03:41,370
Fine.

41
00:03:50,000 --> 00:03:51,300
Your call.

42
00:03:51,600 --> 00:03:54,400
Leave my name on it.

43
00:04:01,000 --> 00:04:04,300
National desk. They want a meeting.

44
00:04:04,600 --> 00:04:07,400
Tomorrow? I can do tomorrow.

45
00:04:10,000 --> 00:04:15,700
Find out who handled these cases. Preserve the access records.

46
00:04:20,000 --> 00:04:24,700
I'm still here. Should I bring someone?

47
00:04:29,000 --> 00:04:31,750
Am I supposed to keep working tonight?

48
00:04:32,050 --> 00:04:35,970
Save what you're doing. We'll arrange a time with counsel.

49
00:04:36,270 --> 00:04:40,580
Email me the request. I want to know what I'm answering.

50
00:04:49,000 --> 00:04:56,200
We need to know where the documents went. You can speak to a lawyer first.
